cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "IWAC Sentiment Analysis Visualization"
abstract: >-
  Interactive SvelteKit dashboard for exploring large language model sentiment
  annotations of the Islam West Africa Collection (IWAC), a corpus of 12,356
  francophone West African press articles from 57 newspapers, published between
  1961 and 2025 in Benin, Burkina Faso, Côte d'Ivoire, Niger and Togo. Each
  article is annotated on three dimensions — polarity, subjectivity, and the
  centrality of Islam and Muslims to the article — by three models per
  annotation campaign. Two campaigns are published side by side: the current one
  (GPT-5.6 Luna, Mistral Small 4, DeepSeek v4 Flash) and an archived first
  campaign (GPT-5 mini, Gemini 3 Flash preview, Ministral 14B 2512), retained
  unchanged so figures and citations published from it stay reproducible. The
  dashboard reports each model's distributions, their agreement (Cohen's kappa,
  quadratic-weighted kappa and Fleiss' kappa), where and how they diverge, and
  blind third-party arbiter evaluations of which annotation better fits the
  source text, with geographic and temporal views, a bilingual French/English
  interface, and CSV export.
